  "id": "COMPOUND:26012 - PROTEIN:5940",
  "verbalization": "Vibsanin Q appears to have a target relationship with Carboxylesterase 2 through a series of intermediate entities, including Hepatocyte and SNB-78, which are all targeted by specific compounds. The evidence suggests that Vibsanin Q may act as a modulator of Carboxylesterase 2, potentially through the activation of downstream targets such as 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which in turn targets Carboxylesterase 2. This pathway implies that Vibsanin Q may influence Carboxylesterase 2 activity by engaging in a chain of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to its activation. The presence of multiple targets and the consistent involvement of Carboxylesterase 2 in the pathways suggest a possible role for Vibsanin Q in modulating the activity of this enzyme, possibly through the regulation of its upstream activators. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Vibsanin Q could interact with Carboxylesterase 2, although the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
